00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:08.740 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my name is Frank Canelo I'm the  owner/operator best pizza here in  Williamsburg Brooklyn but basically just  a regular New York's like shop located  you know in the middle of the block  sandwiched in between a church in a  school pretty sleepy block I was born  and raised in Brooklyn and Bensonhurst  my goal was always to have a  neighborhood period and I wanted to do  it very much in the style of the  pizzeria that I grew up going to well we  did the pizza here I wanted to keep it  limited and focused and pay homage to  all of those slices that were kind of a  special side to the Brooklyn it's three  slices that you would always see is the  Sicilian slice the square the regular  round slice and then you had this white  place so we got the pizza slice so the  white pie is made very similar to all of  our pizzas here we take one of our dough  and we basically open it up so it's  about 20 inches we put it on the wood  peel and then from there we start  layering it and the layering process is  really important we take a little bit of  water and sort of with the pastry  brushes go around the crust on the dough  be able to put the sesame seeds around  so during the baking process the sesame  seeds really stay on after that we start  to take the mozzarella cheese that we  make in-house we grated ourselves and  then we put sort of like just a thin  layer of mozzarella cheese because a  couple cheese components so we try to  keep their ratios and even as possible  after the first layer of mozzarella  cheese we take our ricotta cheese and we  started dollop raghava on top of the  mozzarella around the pie once that's  there I teach my guys so that's a follow  of a dollar serve ragazzo without  carmelized onions we top it off with a  little bit of grated pecorino cheese  my family's Sicilian so we try to take  as many nods from Sicilian cuisine this  so we bake it in a wood-fired oven like  the rest of our pizzas and when it comes  out we finish it with some more pecorino  cheese it's like raw and it has  definitely a different flavor to it and  then a little bit of parsley on top and  I think the parsley adds freshness and  kind of liven it up a little bit our  goal is just always kind of off-duty a  traditional by the slice pizza but make  sure that we're really structure the  traditions in the grating reading  there's something special about the  white pie it just seems to be one of  those pies that people keep coming back  [Music]

